From the Research Engine audit (docs/RESEARCH-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-10-08.md, section K, Phase 2), on top of Phase 1.

Semantic resolution (packages/engine/src/nlSemantics.ts): population phrases
("respondents under 25", "women", "Brand A users", "those who switched",
compounds) become the question and the condition that selects them — on a
numeric age the sentence's own comparator, on age bands the whole bands
inside the range with a straddling band refused and the fix named; concepts
("brand preference", "age") become the variable that measures them (code,
variable, construct, tag, then wording by word families; equal fits are
ambiguous); structural roles ("the screener", "demographics", "this
question", a block); scale descriptions ("5-point", "7-point agree–
disagree", "1 to 10", "0–10 where 0 = …", NPS, yes/no) become points, start
and anchors. The concept families moved here from the measures recogniser.

Recognisers (nlIntent.ts): the screener exclusion in six phrasings
(add_skip to a screened end on the question that learns it; "only allow"
inverted; a twin rule said as already there; two age questions → a choice
each a sentence the engine reads), the scale change (update_question.scale
on the selection, by code or by description; a text question converted; a
multi-select refused with the single-select conversion offered; already so
detected), the crosstab (add_crosstab from two concepts, the demographic in
the banner unless "X by Y" was said; a sentence with a second instruction
left to the model), the most important crosstabs (the framework's
hypothesis-linked, priority-1 tables planned; listed when asked which), the
questions not connected to any hypothesis (answered from the design with
the roles that explain the expected ones), the research objective by
sentence. A model hand-off now carries what the engine can do without one:
standard items for "add a question to measure <X>" and the objective for
"create a research design for <Y>", as executable sentences.

Studio: the failed model turn shows the engine's fallback choices; once the
Studio knows there is no model, such a sentence is an engine question with
the choices and no call is made; after an unusable answer the fallback card
stands instead of the grammar's guess. The change plan
(lib/copilot/changePlan.ts, the turn route, useCopilot, CopilotCard): a
generation is planned first — one schema-bound call for a plan of items with
objects and reasons, the model's questions and assumptions — shown as a
CHANGE PLAN card, ticked and approved; the approved items are built one
schema-bound call each and merged into one proposal through the same gate;
an item that fails is reported and the rest still land; "Plan first" is a
header toggle (on by default, kept per browser). A scripted reply that is
not plan-shaped falls through to the direct turn, so every existing suite
runs unchanged.

Tests: engine nlSemantics.test.ts (7) and nlPhase2.test.ts (7), studio
changePlan.test.ts (3), browser scripts/phase2-nl-test.mjs (13 checks);
phase1-reliability and analysis-framework suites adjusted for behaviour
this phase changed on purpose. Mutation checks: engine 36/36, Studio
surfaces 13/13. Full corpus: 118 ok, the 10 known baseline failures only
(4 need Postgres, 6 unchanged). pnpm -r test green (17 packages), both
typechecks and the auth-guard audit clean.

